    "title": "Yankees' Aaron Judge injury news keeps getting worse - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Billy Heyen ,\n11 minutes ago\nAaron Judge went for imaging on his right ribcage on Wednesday.\nApparently, that wasn't enough for the New York Yankees ' 6-foot-7 superstar.\nHe'll be going to get more tests done, and that can't be good.\nIf the first images were just clear, that'd be it, right? Something must be still a worry.\nMORE: Outfielder retires from baseball to go play college football\nJudge has been out of the Yankees' lineup on both Tuesday and Wednesday against the Cleveland Guardians .\nThe longer this testing period goes on, the more likely it seems that he ends up on the Injured List.\nFor now, the Yankees are just trying to put the pieces together while they wait to see what happens with Judge.\nThere wasn't one obvious moment when Judge got hurt, but he's a big fella who jumps and dives to make strong plays in right field, and there are certainly chances to get dinged up on plays like that.\nThe Yankees can't really afford to lose Judge's presence from their lineup, but he's also been struggling for a bit, potentially playing hurt already.\nFor the sake of their season, they have to get this solved.\nMore MLB news:",
    "summary": "Aaron Judge went for imaging on his right ribcage on Wednesday. MORE: Outfielder retires from baseball to go play college football Judge has been out of the Yankees' lineup on both Tuesday and Wednesday against the Cleveland Guardians . The longer this testing period goes on, the more likely it seems that he ends up on the Injured List. There wasn't one obvious moment when Judge got hurt, but he's a big fella who jumps and dives to make strong plays in right field, and there are certainly chances to get dinged up on plays like that.",
